{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2124-04-02 16:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. You're here because your blood sugar was extremely high and you’ve been feeling unwell. Can you tell me what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2124-04-02 16:35:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I’ve been really anxious lately. My sugars were in the 200s this morning, but then they jumped to over 600. I’ve been thirsty, peeing a lot, and I’ve thrown up a few times."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2124-04-02 16:36:25",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. We also saw you had some rectal bleeding in the ER. Did you notice that?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2124-04-02 16:37:05",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, I did have a few loose stools, but I didn’t see blood. I’ve had stomach issues before with my diabetes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2124-04-02 16:38:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we know you have a history of gastroparesis. Right now, your labs show diabetic ketoacidosis, or DKA. That means your body is producing too many ketones because it doesn’t have enough insulin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2124-04-02 16:39:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know I missed a few insulin doses. I was so nauseous I didn’t eat, so I thought I didn’t need it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2124-04-02 16:40:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a common mistake, but even when you’re not eating, your body still needs insulin. We’re starting an insulin drip to bring your levels down safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2124-04-02 16:41:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. I’ve been so dizzy and thirsty. Is that from the DKA?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2124-04-02 16:42:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. DKA causes dehydration and high blood sugar, which leads to thirst, frequent urination, and nausea. We’re giving you IV fluids to help with that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2124-04-02 16:43:25",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. My back’s been hurting too. I usually take oxycodone, but I didn’t want to mix it with everything else."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2124-04-02 16:44:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll manage your pain with safer options like Tylenol and ibuprofen. We’re avoiding narcotics unless absolutely necessary."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2124-04-02 16:45:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s fine. I just want to feel better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2124-04-03 08:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your blood sugar has come down to 280, and your ketones are improving. We’re transitioning you from the insulin drip to subcutaneous insulin."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2124-04-03 08:16:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. I haven’t vomited since last night. Can I eat something?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2124-04-03 08:17:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll start you on a diabetic diet. Small, frequent meals are best. We’re also checking your thiamine levels."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2124-04-03 08:18:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thiamine? Why?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2124-04-03 08:19:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Because people with poor nutrition and chronic illness, especially with vomiting, can become deficient. We found yours was low, so we’re starting supplements."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2124-04-03 08:20:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. I haven’t been eating much. Thank you for catching that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2124-04-04 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did an abdominal X-ray yesterday. It showed a lack of bowel gas, which is common in gastroparesis. No blockage, so that’s reassuring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2124-04-04 09:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So that’s why I feel so full and nauseous?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2124-04-04 09:02:05",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your stomach is emptying slowly. That’s why we’re holding off on metoclopramide for now — we want to see if your DKA improvement helps your stomach function."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2124-04-04 09:03:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. My anxiety’s been worse too. I’ve been on sertraline, but it doesn’t feel like it’s helping."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2124-04-04 09:04:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Psychiatry reviewed your case. They recommend increasing your sertraline to 100 mg daily. We’ll also keep your lorazepam for breakthrough anxiety."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2124-04-04 09:05:45",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll try that. I just don’t want to keep ending up here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2124-04-04 09:06:30",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re setting you up with endocrinology and your psychiatrist after discharge. But we also need you to follow up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2124-04-04 09:07:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I know, but I’ve been overwhelmed. I’ll try."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2124-04-05 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood sugar spiked again last night, and your acid levels started to rise. We had to restart the insulin drip."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2124-04-05 10:31:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m so frustrated. I thought I was getting better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2124-04-05 10:32:05",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s okay. This is common in DKA recovery. We’re adjusting your insulin regimen. We’ll try glargine at night and a sliding scale for meals."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2124-04-05 10:33:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will that help me avoid the ICU again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2124-04-05 10:34:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We hope so. We’re also adding dextrose to your IV to prevent low blood sugar while you’re not eating well."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2124-04-06 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news — your DKA has resolved. Your last blood sugar was 150, and you’ve kept down breakfast."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2124-04-06 08:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Really? That’s a relief. Can I go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2124-04-06 08:02:05",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not yet. We want to make sure your sugars stay stable. We’re increasing your glargine to 25 units at night to see how you do."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2124-04-06 08:03:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, but I’ve had lows before with higher doses."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2124-04-06 08:04:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll monitor closely. If you have morning lows, we’ll lower it back. Safety first."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2124-04-07 07:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We had to lower your glargine back to 20 units. You had a fasting glucose of 60 this morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2124-04-07 07:46:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I felt shaky. I’m glad you caught it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2124-04-07 07:47:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll keep it at 20 units. If your morning sugars are over 140, you can increase by 2 units every two days until they improve."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2124-04-07 07:48:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’ll write that down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2124-04-07 14:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re also starting lidocaine patches for your back pain. They’re safer than narcotics long-term."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2124-04-07 14:21:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve used them before. They help. Can I also take ibuprofen?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2124-04-07 14:22:05",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, up to 400 mg every 8 hours as needed. Just not on an empty stomach."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2124-04-08 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your labs are stable. No infection was found — blood and urine cultures were clean."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2124-04-08 09:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. I was worried about that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2124-04-08 09:02:05",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow if all goes well. You’ll follow up with GI for your nausea and your psychiatrist for your anxiety."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2124-04-08 09:03:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I have an appointment with my psychiatrist already?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2124-04-08 09:04:10",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s scheduled. And endocrinology wants you to call them to set up a visit."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2124-04-08 09:05:25",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll do my best. I know I need to take better care of myself."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2124-04-09 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re placing a PICC line today so you can get IV fluids at home if needed, just in case."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2124-04-09 10:01:15",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that necessary? I’m feeling much better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2124-04-09 10:02:05",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s a precaution. If you can’t keep fluids down again, you can get treated at home instead of coming back here."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2124-04-09 10:03:20",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2124-04-09 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The PICC line was placed successfully. You’re doing well. We’ll remove the IV and prepare for discharge tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2124-04-09 15:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. Can you go over my new medications again?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2124-04-09 15:02:25",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Of course. You’ll take 20 units of glargine at bedtime. Increase by 2 units every two days if your morning sugar is over 140."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2124-04-09 15:03:40",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And the fast-acting insulin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2124-04-09 15:04:15",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Use your aspart per the sliding scale based on your fingerstick. Stop the metoclopramide. Take sertraline 100 mg daily, thiamine 100 mg daily, and use the lidocaine patch as needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2124-04-09 15:05:30",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. No more reglan. I’ll take notes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2124-04-10 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re cleared to go home. You’re doing well — alert, eating, and your sugars are stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2124-04-10 09:01:10",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you so much. I’ll try to follow up and take better care of myself."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2124-04-10 09:02:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re here to help. Call your doctors, check your sugars regularly, and don’t skip insulin — even if you’re not eating."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2124-04-10 09:03:35",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I promise. I don’t want to be back here again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2124-04-10 09:04:20",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll send all instructions and prescriptions with you. Take care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2124-04-10 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2124-04-02 16:34:00",
    "admission_end": "2124-04-10 15:15:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with type 1 diabetes, anxiety, and gastroparesis was admitted for diabetic ketoacidosis triggered by insulin nonadherence amid worsening nausea and vomiting. She presented with severe hyperglycemia, dehydration, and abdominal discomfort. Treated initially in the MICU with an insulin drip and IV fluids, she had transient improvement but required re-initiation of the drip due to recurrent DKA. Her nausea resolved as her metabolic state stabilized, and she transitioned to subcutaneous insulin. Thiamine deficiency was identified and treated. Glargine was titrated but reduced due to fasting hypoglycemia. Anxiety was addressed with increased sertraline and continued lorazepam. Chronic back pain was managed with non-opioid therapies. She was discharged home with medication adjustments, including increased sertraline, thiamine supplementation, lidocaine patches, and a revised insulin regimen, along with follow-up plans for endocrinology, psychiatry, and GI.",
    "problems": [
      "Diabetes with ketoacidosis, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Other and unspecified manifestations of thiamine deficiency",
      "Diabetes with renal manifestations, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Long-term (current) use of insulin",
      "Dysthymic disorder",
      "Panic disorder without agoraphobia",
      "Lumbago",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Personal history of noncompliance with medical treatment, presenting hazards to health"
    ]
  }
}
